  "id": "visuospatial-function",
  "term": "visuospatial function",
  "definition": "Visuospatial function is the brain’s processing of visual information about space and spatial relationships in the environment. In this source, it refers to a network involving fronto-parieto-occipital areas and the thalamus that helps interpret visual stimuli, direct attention to their significance, and shape emotional and behavioral responses to what is seen.",
